      "title": "Casual Grounds Crew",
      "description": "Casual Grounds Crew | Career Opportunities Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post Casual Grounds Crew Job Category : Facilities Management Requisition Number : CASUA001547 Apply now Posting Details Posted : March 25, 2026 Full-Time On-site Locations Showing 1 location Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description Position Title: Casual Grounds Crew Department: Facilities Management Position Type: Casual Classification: UNIFOR, IA1 Salary Range: $19.39 Position Overview StFX University is seeking dependable, hard-working applicants for Casual Grounds Crew positions within Facilities Management – Grounds & Transport. Successful candidates will support year-round grounds and landscape maintenance activities, contributing to the overall appearance, safety, and functionality of campus outdoor spaces. This role offers hands-on, physically active work in a team-oriented environment, with responsibilities that vary seasonally based on operational and weather-related needs. Salary is in accordance with the UNIFOR collective agreement. IA1 rate is $19.39/hour. Hours are variable and operationally driven, scheduled on an “as needed” basis (days, evenings, nights, and weekends). Key Responsibilities Perform a variety of grounds maintenance duties to support a clean, safe, and well-maintained campus. This position is physically demanding, requiring regular bending, kneeling, standing, lifting, pushing, pulling, and squatting. Work is performed outdoors in varying weather conditions throughout the year. Garbage and litter pick-up across campus grounds. Mowing, trimming, and edging lawns and landscaped areas. Operating grounds equipment including push mowers, riding mowers, zero-turn mowers, trimmers, and leaf blowers. Leaf blowing and seasonal clean-up of walkways, lawns, and landscaped areas. Assisting with planting, digging, mulching, and general horticultural maintenance. Transporting tools, materials, soil, mulch, and other grounds supplies. Performing basic cleaning and care of grounds equipment and reporting mechanical or safety concerns. Maintaining safe and accessible walkways, entrances, and outdoor areas. Reporting unsafe conditions or equipment issues to a supervisor. Other related duties as assigned. During the winter season , responsibilities also include: Snow removal by shovel and/or snow blower. Ice control, including salting, chipping, and other manual methods. Clearing walkways, building entrances, stairways, and emergency exits. Assisting with refilling salt bins and moving winter maintenance materials. Employees are required to wear appropriate personal protective equipment, including CSA-approved safety footwear (loaners available if required), and dress appropriately for outdoor working conditions. Qualifications Previous experience in grounds maintenance, landscaping, or horticulture is an asset. Experience operating grounds equipment (e.g., zero-turn mowers, tractors, trimmers) is considered a strong asset. Strong work ethic and willingness to perform physically demanding work. Reliable, punctual, and able to respond to operational needs, including short-notice work. Ability to follow instructions and work independently or as part of a team Good communication and organizational skills. Orientation and job-specific training will be provided to successful candidates. To apply for this opportunity, click the \"Apply Now\" button and upload your cover letter, resume and references. StFX is located in Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq People. StFX is committed to equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility and encourages applications from individuals who will contribute to the diversity of our community. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. StFX is also committed to eliminating barriers to participation for persons with disabilities. If accommodation is required during the recruitment process, please contact People and Culture at hr@stfx.ca or 902-867-5038. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications St. Francis Xavier University You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
